          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is \(50\).</para>
            <para>The correct answer is is \(n\). The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is \(50\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_7fc8f227-f6be-48a3-97bf-c9787f891f76" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para> For the equation \(y=-(x+100)^2+50\), does the graph open up or down?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The graph opens downward. The squared term has a negative coefficient \((-1)\)..</para>
            <para>Incorrect. The correct answer is Up. The graph opens downward. The squared term has a negative coefficient \((-1)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
