        <exercise id="_10468be6-f473-420b-b5a3-b14329156584" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para> For the equation \(y=a(x+m)^2+n\), can you determine if the graph opens up or down with the information you are given?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! No, because the direction of opening depends on whether \(a\) is positive or negative.</para>
            <para>Incorrect. No, because the direction of opening depends on whether \(a\) is positive or negative.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
